  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assisting the conservation status and needs of eastern bonobos (Pan paniscus) living in a savannah-forest mosaic in the Lac Tumba Landscape, DRC.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this 1-year project is to protect bonobos in the southwestern section of the Lac Tumba landscape by determining their conservation status and needs, and identifying sub-populations for regular monitoring. Specific activities include: 1) determining bonobo population size and distribution in the project zone; and 2) improving knowledge of the threats to those populations.</narrative>
  </description>
